From e9d537b75ab6bd34c189e2e3d5dd005717c2711f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:02:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] move guard: one git deadline per tree scan;
 'unchecked' cause and state_parts case (PR #1792 review nits)

Follow-up t_01a1d427faa4ce9b to PR #1792 (reviews t_01a1d41a33521f17 / 5888531766 and
t_01a1d2a839617871 / 5885034090). Rebased onto e370f8ee4b (card t_01a1d2add77deeff), which
landed items 3-5 first: its shared repin leaving rule (kanban_move.leaves_here/_repin_leaves)
and park-path test are kept as they are; its _BudgetSpent/_within/found() cause handling in
tree_state is replaced by the GitBudget below, which covers every git call, not only the
three top-level checks. Its tests (test_kanban_move_guard_review_nits.py) pass unchanged.

1. STATE_BUDGET_S was approximate: tree_state handed out per-helper timeouts, but the
   no-remote-refs path of _worktree_has_unpushed_commits made up to 5 calls on one timeout,
   and _worktree_is_dirty's noninteractive_repo_git_env probes (2 s each, up to 18) and
   hidden_index_edits (120 s ls-files, 60 s hash-object) ran outside the deadline. New
   hermes_cli/git_budget.py: a GitBudget callable (cap -> timeout drawn from one deadline,
   raises GitUnchecked once spent). _worktree_is_dirty, _worktree_has_unpushed_commits,
   _worktree_local_trunk, noninteractive_repo_git_env, worktree_archive._env and
   hidden_index_edits take an optional keyword `budget`; tree_state and pushed_on_remote
   thread one budget through every git call. Without a budget nothing changes for the
   other callers.
2. state_parts() recognises 'unchecked worktree <p> (<cause>)' -> ('unchecked', <p>), so a
   budget-spent park pin records check/tree.
3. GitUnchecked is not a ValueError/SubprocessError: budget exhaustion inside
   pushed_on_remote reads 'unchecked worktree <p>' instead of 'unpushed commits in <p>', and
   a git timeout (or a hardening probe with no answer) in a budgeted dirty check reads
   'unchecked worktree <p> (git timed out)' instead of 'dirty worktree'. Still state (fail
   safe). An unreachable remote within budget still reads 'unpushed'.
4. On main already (e370f8ee4b unified the repin with check()'s leaving rule); this
   commit's earlier docstring/test for the old exact-label rule were dropped in the rebase.
5. Park-path test for the kanban_continue path (main's covers kanban_block): a park naming
   another card's owner-marked tree with unpushed commits does not pin; the owner's own
   park still does.

RED (fix reverted, new tests kept, pre-rebase): 7 of the new tests failed (hung ls-files
ran to fake t=32 s > 20 s; 12 trees of slow probes overran a 5 s budget; the no-remote path
read 'unpushed'; a status timeout read 'dirty'; state_parts and the park pin returned
check='').
GREEN after the rebase: test_kanban_move_guard_budget.py (13) + test_kanban_move_guard_review_nits.py
(9) pass, and all 77 test files importing the changed helpers: 2177 passed, 0 failed, 159 skipped.
